<div id="2026-11-09-apk-download-endpoint" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-09 — APK download route with the Android package MIME type</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> New public <code>GET /api/app/download</code> streams the current inventory APK with <code>Content-Type: application/vnd.android.package-archive</code> and <code>Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="ComservInventory.apk"</code>. It serves <code>/data/nfs/inventory-apks/ComservInventory.apk</code> and falls back to <code>root/static/app/ComservInventory.apk</code>; when neither is readable it answers JSON 404 instead of an HTML error page. <code>root/static/app/version.json</code> now points <code>apkUrl</code> at this route (versionCode 7, versionName 1.6). Static <code>.apk</code> serving also declares the package MIME type, so a direct <code>/static/app/...</code> link downloads instead of opening as text.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The phone app updater follows <code>apkUrl</code> from <code>/api/app/version</code>. The Gradle <code>publishToNfs</code> task in <code>comserv-inventory-android</code> writes <code>/home/shanta/nfs/inventory-apks/version.json</code> (same directory as <code>/data/nfs/inventory-apks</code>, one NFS export) with <code>apkUrl: /static/app/ComservInventory.apk</code>, so phones already in the field point at the static path. Without an APK MIME type that path was served as unknown content and the updater could not install it; the web copy's <code>apkUrl</code> now names the route instead. Both URLs resolve to the same NFS file.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Who owns which file.</strong> Gradle writes only the NFS <code>version.json</code>; nothing in this app copies it into <code>root/static/app/version.json</code>, so the web copy stays hand-maintained and is what <code>/api/app/version</code> serves.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm</code> (<code>api_app_download</code>), <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv.pm</code> (<code>Static::Simple</code> <code>mime_types</code>), <code>Comserv/root/static/app/version.json</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified 2026-11-09</strong> against the running :3001 instance: <code>curl -D -</code> returned 200, <code>Content-Type: application/vnd.android.package-archive</code>, <code>Content-Length: 35099202</code>, and <code>/api/app/version</code> returned 200 JSON.</p>
</div>
